<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Mainland Southeast Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">Thonburi Kingdom</h1><p class="st-meta">1767 CE – 1782 CE · capital Thonburi</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The kingdom of Taksin, who reunited Siam within a few years of Ayutthaya's destruction and ruled from Thonburi on the Chao Phraya.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taksin">Taksin</a>, a provincial governor of part-Chinese descent, broke out of besieged <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/ayutthaya-kingdom">Ayutthaya</a> in 1767, gathered forces in the south-east at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chanthaburi">Chanthaburi</a> and drove the Burmese garrison from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ayutthaya-kingdom">Ayutthaya</a> area later that year. He chose Thonburi, a fortified town downriver, as his capital and was crowned king.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Between 1768 and 1770 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taksin">Taksin</a> defeated the rival regimes of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/phimai">Phimai</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/phitsanulok">Phitsanulok</a>, Sawangkhaburi and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nakhon-si-thammarat">Nakhon Si Thammarat</a>. His generals, the brothers <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rama-i">Chao Phraya Chakri</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maha-sura-singhanat">Surasi</a>, expelled the Burmese from <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/lan-na">Lan Na</a> and conquered the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-vientiane">Kingdom of Vientiane</a> in 1779, bringing back the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emerald-buddha">Emerald Buddha</a>. Taksin encouraged Chinese trade and settlement to rebuild the economy.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In his later years <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taksin">Taksin</a> was said to have become religiously obsessive and erratic. A revolt in 1782 deposed him, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rama-i">Chao Phraya Chakri</a> returned from <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-cambodia-1953-1970">Cambodia</a>, had Taksin executed and became <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rama">Rama</a> I, founding the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/rattanakosin-kingdom">Rattanakosin Kingdom</a> and moving the capital across the river to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bangkok">Bangkok</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/thonburi-kingdom.jpg" alt="Thonburi Kingdom" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Xiengyod · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Thailand_(Ayutthaya_period).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1767 CE – 1782 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Thonburi</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Taksin</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Theravada Buddhism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Thai</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/thailand">Thailand</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Thonburi, Siam</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1774&amp;focus=thonburi-kingdom" aria-label="Thonburi Kingdom on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="7433 1667 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Thonburi Kingdom lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M7753 1923L7762 2119M7753 1923L7697 1683M7753 1923L7799 1867M7753 1923L7752 1900M7753 1923L7567 1068M7753 1923L7754 1922M7753 1923L7756 1697M7753 1923L7784 1767M7753 1923L7894 1880"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7762 2119h0M7697 1683h0M7799 1867h0M7752 1900h0M7567 1068h0M7754 1922h0M7756 1697h0M7784 1767h0M7894 1880h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7753 1923h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7753 1923h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its capital. <a href="/atlas?year=1774&amp;focus=thonburi-kingdom">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
